  "limitations": [
    "Local Wi-Fi carrier to pinned Xray-core; synthetic IPv4/IPv6 destinations redirect to local backends.",
    "HTTP 204 is availability, not TCP byte integrity. UDP nonce query/response is 67/83 bytes, not an MTU sweep.",
    "Resource loads are finite request bursts, not sustained bulk transfer, five-sample calibrated gates or Go/sing-box performance comparisons.",
    "RSS is sampled and CPU is the full host process; no continuous peak, energy or formal Perfetto claim.",
    "Connecting cancellation is not complete cancel-active-flow coverage. Close/recovery is independently probed.",
    "No Android WAN transitions, lock/wake, shared legacy matrix or formal schema-4 archive in this report.",
    "Trojan and SS2022 AES-128 UDP request stress have retained timeouts. Correlated backend replies precede the client timeout; the core decoded-UDP counter misses one response. The exact cause is unresolved; reordered controls pass on both paths.",
    "Initial full-VPN resource attempt includes background app traffic. Controlled resource observations use the separate probe UID only, with distinct APK identities.",
    "PacketPump consumes about one core at idle: xray-tun-in spins on zero-byte nonblocking reads. This baseline is not acceptable idle CPU behavior; see the separate readiness-wait follow-up.",
    "The hard-coded unrecoveredTransitions telemetry value is not used as evidence of real recovery.",
    "Historical SS2022 WAN losses are deferred, not fixed or erased."
